1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:40,830
Hey, you guys.

2
00:01:41,270 --> 00:01:42,670
Are we sure this is the right way?

3
00:01:42,930 --> 00:01:44,610
Yep, this is correct.

4
00:01:45,410 --> 00:01:47,330
According to our trusty map,

5
00:01:47,570 --> 00:01:49,870
these stairs should lead right to the fifth floor,

6
00:01:50,070 --> 00:01:50,870
near the orc settlement.

7
00:01:53,350 --> 00:01:55,270
Seems pretty sketchy.

8
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:57,870
This is amazing.

9
00:01:57,870 --> 00:02:00,090
Look at all these different tentacles.

10
00:02:00,770 --> 00:02:03,230
The orcs must have pulled a fast one on us.

11
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:05,230
There's no way they would leave this be.

12
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:06,010
I don't know.

13
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:08,410
It does connect to their settlement.

14
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:10,750
Makes sense they'd want to keep people out.

15
00:02:12,490 --> 00:02:14,430
Let's press on for now.

16
00:02:15,390 --> 00:02:17,630
I think it would save us time and energy

17
00:02:17,630 --> 00:02:19,350
if we just found a different way.

18
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:22,830
Careful.

19
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:25,050
Don't get too close to the wall.

20
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:29,130
These monsters like to hide their bodies inside of them.

21
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:32,790
Lots of tentacles usually means that the walls are hollowed out.

22
00:02:33,490 --> 00:02:35,410
Those things love to set up camp in there.

23
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:37,430
They interfere with devices,

24
00:02:37,850 --> 00:02:38,950
grow on treasure chests,

25
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:41,370
and are just a general pain in the ass.

26
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:44,590
I hate them almost as much as I hate mimics.

27
00:02:44,590 --> 00:02:46,870
There.

28
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:49,750
I think we've made very good progress.

29
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:55,310
That's weird.

30
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:57,090
The orcs should have passed through here

31
00:02:57,090 --> 00:02:58,190
to get to the third floor.

32
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:00,550
But how'd they get through all this?

33
00:03:01,750 --> 00:03:02,010
Huh?

34
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:03,330
Something's here.

35
00:03:03,730 --> 00:03:04,230
Be careful.

36
00:03:04,230 --> 00:03:04,310
Be careful.

37
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:13,870
Kinsuke!

38
00:03:14,270 --> 00:03:15,470
A giant frog?

39
00:03:15,750 --> 00:03:17,110
A grove!

40
00:03:17,670 --> 00:03:18,090
No!

41
00:03:18,510 --> 00:03:19,470
What have you done?

42
00:03:19,830 --> 00:03:20,650
Stand back!

43
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:21,530
Last lap!

44
00:03:27,530 --> 00:03:27,890
Hey!

45
00:03:27,890 --> 00:03:28,530
Hey!

46
00:03:30,530 --> 00:03:31,090
Abrosia!

47
00:03:31,090 --> 00:03:31,170
Abrosia!

48
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:31,730
Abrosia!

49
00:03:34,310 --> 00:03:35,310
Abrosia!

50
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:37,870
Abrosia!

51
00:03:37,870 --> 00:03:38,310
Abrosia!

52
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:40,030
Senchi!

53
00:03:40,230 --> 00:03:40,790
Behind you!

54
00:03:44,830 --> 00:03:46,270
Don't let go, okay?

55
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:47,750
Do you have a plan?

56
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:50,510
My magic should do the trick!

57
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:50,930
No!

58
00:03:51,050 --> 00:03:51,790
We're too close!

59
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:53,070
This is bad.

60
00:03:53,630 --> 00:03:54,610
What should we do?

61
00:03:56,130 --> 00:03:56,770
Wait.

62
00:03:57,330 --> 00:03:58,310
That tentacle...

63
00:03:59,210 --> 00:04:01,170
There's something about it seems...

64
00:04:01,170 --> 00:04:01,970
out of place.

65
00:04:01,970 --> 00:04:04,610
I'll bet it's all tangled up in a trap.

66
00:04:05,310 --> 00:04:07,950
I wonder if there's any way I could make use of that.

67
00:04:08,970 --> 00:04:09,810
But how?

68
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:11,450
If I touch it directly,

69
00:04:11,830 --> 00:04:13,810
I'll be in for a world of hurt.

70
00:04:15,810 --> 00:04:15,950
Huh?

71
00:04:17,950 --> 00:04:18,930
Hey, Lyos!

72
00:04:19,210 --> 00:04:19,550
Huh?

73
00:04:19,710 --> 00:04:22,950
Why don't the tentacles seem to be hurting the giant frogs at all?

74
00:04:22,950 --> 00:04:23,350
Oh!

75
00:04:24,650 --> 00:04:25,290
Uh...

76
00:04:25,290 --> 00:04:26,430
I don't know.

77
00:04:26,510 --> 00:04:27,630
That's just how they're made?

78
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:31,270
Real helpful, Mr. Monsterpedia!

79
00:04:31,510 --> 00:04:33,770
Ah, the curiosity of youth.

80
00:04:34,770 --> 00:04:35,770
Ah, whatever.

81
00:04:40,770 --> 00:04:41,410
Uh...

82
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:49,310
Wait, what are you doing?

83
00:04:49,310 --> 00:04:55,090
It doesn't hurt.

84
00:04:55,290 --> 00:04:56,170
I can do this!

85
00:04:57,290 --> 00:04:58,650
What the...

86
00:04:58,650 --> 00:05:01,110
It won't come out!

87
00:05:06,950 --> 00:05:07,870
Come on!

88
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,610
Kill Chuck!

89
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:10,030
No!

90
00:05:10,030 --> 00:05:10,230
No!

91
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:10,730
No!

92
00:05:10,730 --> 00:05:10,830
No!

93
00:05:10,830 --> 00:05:11,090
No!

94
00:05:11,090 --> 00:05:11,150
No!

95
00:05:11,150 --> 00:05:11,210
No!

96
00:05:21,210 --> 00:05:21,790
No!

97
00:05:21,790 --> 00:05:22,290
No!

98
00:05:22,290 --> 00:05:23,270
Quick, let's get him out!

99
00:05:28,710 --> 00:05:29,230
Phew!

100
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:30,110
He's alive.

101
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:30,910
Show me your hands!

102
00:05:31,710 --> 00:05:32,270
No way!

103
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:33,110
They're not hurt?

104
00:05:33,690 --> 00:05:34,610
This frogskin,

105
00:05:34,890 --> 00:05:37,150
you used it like gloves to protect your hands.

106
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:38,770
That's really smart.

107
00:05:42,850 --> 00:05:43,490
Chill Chuck.

108
00:05:44,650 --> 00:05:46,810
This here is a great idea.

109
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:50,430
Start an incision at its belly

110
00:05:50,430 --> 00:05:52,730
and completely skin the frog.

111
00:05:53,730 --> 00:05:55,190
Uh, hang on, I...

112
00:05:55,190 --> 00:05:56,890
For the tentacles, peel the skin.

113
00:05:57,450 --> 00:05:57,750
Huh?

114
00:05:57,930 --> 00:05:59,730
Gather the parts that have thin tips,

115
00:05:59,970 --> 00:06:00,670
set them aside,

116
00:06:01,070 --> 00:06:02,530
and boil the thicker parts.

117
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:04,090
Once done,

118
00:06:04,390 --> 00:06:06,110
mash them up and mix them with flour.

119
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:08,150
Shape them into cylinders

120
00:06:08,150 --> 00:06:09,950
and gently press with a fork,

121
00:06:10,410 --> 00:06:11,910
then boil once more.

122
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:12,610
Tenshi!

123
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:15,110
Hang the skins of the giant frogs to dry,

124
00:06:15,730 --> 00:06:16,650
take measurements,

125
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:18,230
and begin sewing.

126
00:06:18,650 --> 00:06:19,590
Add olive oil,

127
00:06:20,270 --> 00:06:21,510
garlic and chili peppers,

128
00:06:22,170 --> 00:06:23,610
then the frog leg meat.

129
00:06:23,950 --> 00:06:24,890
Fry it all up,

130
00:06:24,890 --> 00:06:25,730
and...

131
00:06:25,730 --> 00:06:27,050
It's ready!

132
00:06:30,050 --> 00:06:32,090
I can't believe these guys!

133
00:06:32,650 --> 00:06:34,170
Could you both take turns?

134
00:06:34,350 --> 00:06:36,250
Before I could even pick who to stop first,

135
00:06:36,310 --> 00:06:37,010
it was too late!

136
00:06:37,510 --> 00:06:38,610
Don't be like that.

137
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:39,550
Just try it on.

138
00:06:39,770 --> 00:06:40,670
Yes, yes.

139
00:06:40,730 --> 00:06:42,470
Come on, go and take a little bite.

140
00:06:42,590 --> 00:06:44,510
I told you to take turns!

141
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:47,350
No way you're getting me to wear that.

142
00:06:51,550 --> 00:06:53,330
If you wore this, Marcille,

143
00:06:53,510 --> 00:06:55,030
we think you'd look real cute.

144
00:06:55,030 --> 00:07:10,670
It's great, really!

145
00:07:10,890 --> 00:07:12,350
What a nice color on you.

146
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:13,910
So neat how the eye parts

147
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:15,290
make it look like we have little ears.

148
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:16,770
Let's go.

149
00:07:17,670 --> 00:07:18,190
Yes, ma'am.

150
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:23,470
Amazing!

151
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:24,890
It doesn't hurt a bit!

152
00:07:25,110 --> 00:07:27,550
This stuff is giving me the heebie-jeebies!

153
00:07:28,210 --> 00:07:29,490
So beautiful.

154
00:07:30,790 --> 00:07:31,470
And yummy!

155
00:07:37,470 --> 00:07:38,350
Kensuke!

156
00:07:39,150 --> 00:07:39,870
Ambrosia!

157
00:07:42,190 --> 00:07:42,870
Guys?

158
00:07:43,810 --> 00:07:45,370
The castle town.

159
00:07:45,790 --> 00:07:47,930
We're already on the fifth floor.

160
00:07:48,190 --> 00:07:54,750
Looks like they left in a hurry.

161
00:07:55,610 --> 00:07:57,970
So the orcs were telling the truth then.

162
00:07:58,470 --> 00:08:01,550
And that means the red dragon can't be far off.

163
00:08:02,170 --> 00:08:03,150
Let's stay on our guard

164
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:04,530
and see what else we can find here.

165
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:05,590
Right.

166
00:08:07,050 --> 00:08:07,750
Hey, uh...

167
00:08:08,470 --> 00:08:09,650
Laios?

168
00:08:10,270 --> 00:08:11,670
Is this frog blood?

169
00:08:12,050 --> 00:08:13,490
It hardened onto my clothes

170
00:08:13,490 --> 00:08:15,490
and now I can't get this thing off of me.

171
00:08:16,110 --> 00:08:17,950
It's because I didn't really have the time

172
00:08:17,950 --> 00:08:19,090
to completely tan it.

173
00:08:19,810 --> 00:08:21,790
We're fighting the dragon like this?

174
00:08:24,510 --> 00:08:25,730
Forget the dragon!

175
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:28,390
How am I going to look felon in the eyes, huh?

176
00:08:28,990 --> 00:08:30,210
Answer me!

177
00:08:30,210 --> 00:08:47,230
My insides don't feel so good.

178
00:08:47,470 --> 00:08:50,110
Kiki, Kaka, show Namari to the guest room.

179
00:08:50,110 --> 00:08:55,450
While you do that, I will go and report to the island lord.

180
00:09:02,530 --> 00:09:05,150
So, how was the dungeon?

181
00:09:05,150 --> 00:09:10,690
The thing to be most concerned about is it has become more perilous.

182
00:09:11,090 --> 00:09:14,390
Treasure down to the third floor has been stripped bare.

183
00:09:14,830 --> 00:09:16,930
Hideouts for outlaws are on the rise.

184
00:09:17,490 --> 00:09:20,530
And orcs have been appearing on the upper floors

185
00:09:20,530 --> 00:09:23,430
and are frequently causing problems.

186
00:09:23,430 --> 00:09:26,230
I would suggest sending in troops

187
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:27,810
or offering a bounty.

188
00:09:29,090 --> 00:09:32,070
How do they even manage to find their way in?

189
00:09:32,510 --> 00:09:35,810
Perhaps the pathways were connected from old dwarven tunnels.

190
00:09:36,450 --> 00:09:39,110
Orcs have been known to settle in such places.

191
00:09:39,110 --> 00:09:40,470
Dwarves, you say?

192
00:09:40,670 --> 00:09:42,810
What a truly troublesome lot they are.

193
00:09:43,590 --> 00:09:44,750
They're like moles.

194
00:09:45,010 --> 00:09:47,630
No matter how many holes we close, another pops up.

195
00:09:48,390 --> 00:09:50,890
Long ago, when the elves and dwarves split

196
00:09:50,890 --> 00:09:53,030
between east and west because of a war,

197
00:09:53,350 --> 00:09:55,390
the dwarves hid in these lands,

198
00:09:55,750 --> 00:09:57,350
waiting for the elves to attack.

199
00:09:58,070 --> 00:09:59,470
Even after the war ended,

200
00:09:59,770 --> 00:10:01,390
they continued digging holes,

201
00:10:01,930 --> 00:10:04,570
eventually turning the golden country into a dungeon.

202
00:10:05,130 --> 00:10:08,070
I've even heard that the dungeon continues to grow

203
00:10:08,070 --> 00:10:10,730
because of the descendants of those very dwarves.

204
00:10:11,390 --> 00:10:14,050
Let us move on from unsubstantiated rumors.

205
00:10:14,830 --> 00:10:16,830
Here are the drawings of the magic circles.

206
00:10:17,950 --> 00:10:20,010
They are in the usual eldish language.

207
00:10:20,410 --> 00:10:21,710
And according to the penmanship,

208
00:10:21,910 --> 00:10:23,150
it is the same author.

209
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:25,690
And there are no signs of anyone else

210
00:10:25,690 --> 00:10:27,050
modifying them at all.

211
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:29,430
There's no mistaking it.

212
00:10:29,770 --> 00:10:30,770
The lord of the dungeon,

213
00:10:30,970 --> 00:10:32,590
or should I say the mad mage,

214
00:10:32,690 --> 00:10:34,070
drew these magic circles.

215
00:10:34,470 --> 00:10:36,410
Is this individual an elf?

216
00:10:36,410 --> 00:10:38,290
I cannot say with certainty,

217
00:10:38,610 --> 00:10:41,570
but it's unlikely a tall man or dwarf cast it.

218
00:10:41,990 --> 00:10:43,030
This is concerning.

219
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:44,050
Hmm?

220
00:10:44,510 --> 00:10:46,010
The thing is, the other day,

221
00:10:46,370 --> 00:10:48,730
I received a letter from the elves of the west.

222
00:10:49,350 --> 00:10:49,830
It said,

223
00:10:50,230 --> 00:10:51,870
the dungeon belongs to us.

224
00:10:52,410 --> 00:10:53,190
Relinquish it.

225
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:55,850
How utterly conceited!

226
00:10:56,130 --> 00:10:58,110
They're the ones who gave the lands to the humans

227
00:10:58,110 --> 00:11:01,670
after taking and squandering those lands from the dwarves.

228
00:11:02,110 --> 00:11:03,150
Just ignore them.

229
00:11:03,150 --> 00:11:06,210
This land was bestowed to me by the king of the elves,

230
00:11:06,350 --> 00:11:08,050
so I'm afraid that's not possible.

231
00:11:08,790 --> 00:11:09,190
Hmm.

232
00:11:09,950 --> 00:11:11,910
Now take the entire island.

233
00:11:12,710 --> 00:11:14,110
I certainly hope not.

234
00:11:14,550 --> 00:11:16,810
There is most likely a vast amount of riches

235
00:11:16,810 --> 00:11:18,590
still in the bowels of that dungeon.

236
00:11:18,850 --> 00:11:19,530
My lord,

237
00:11:20,050 --> 00:11:22,570
their objective is not any material treasure,

238
00:11:22,570 --> 00:11:25,830
but the immortality spell cast on the dungeon.

239
00:11:26,510 --> 00:11:28,670
This spell that tethers the soul to the body

240
00:11:28,670 --> 00:11:30,010
is still a great mystery.

241
00:11:30,530 --> 00:11:32,730
And once that mystery becomes unraveled,

242
00:11:32,770 --> 00:11:35,610
its value will far exceed any amount of gold.

243
00:11:36,130 --> 00:11:38,390
We should solve it before the elves do.

244
00:11:38,390 --> 00:11:41,990
So we should trace all of the magic circles and study them?

245
00:11:42,490 --> 00:11:43,570
That's not enough!

246
00:11:44,030 --> 00:11:47,150
A powerful spell such as this is bound to have a schematic.

247
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:48,950
You should seek it out.

248
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,530
After we get our hands on it,

249
00:11:51,830 --> 00:11:53,930
then you can agree to give them back the dungeon.

250
00:11:54,930 --> 00:11:57,990
Once they realize we possess that valuable knowledge,

251
00:11:58,390 --> 00:12:00,130
the elves will see you as an equal.

252
00:12:00,370 --> 00:12:00,890
No.

253
00:12:00,890 --> 00:12:04,350
They will kneel before you to curry your favor.

254
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:06,650
You... you think so?

255
00:12:07,390 --> 00:12:09,130
So where do you think it might be?

256
00:12:09,890 --> 00:12:11,190
Isn't it obvious?

257
00:12:11,830 --> 00:12:14,590
The lord of the dungeon would have possession over it.

258
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:17,910
So we should keep sending in adventurers to search the premises?

259
00:12:18,270 --> 00:12:19,250
That is correct.

260
00:12:19,950 --> 00:12:23,710
Monster extermination and buying artifacts from the dungeon is pivotal.

261
00:12:24,430 --> 00:12:27,250
Spend your coin and aid those adventurers.

262
00:12:28,050 --> 00:12:28,790
I understand.

263
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:31,410
I will put out a reward for the orcs.

264
00:12:31,830 --> 00:12:33,450
And my reply to the elves?

265
00:12:33,830 --> 00:12:36,210
I will pen something that buys us some time.

266
00:12:38,510 --> 00:12:40,310
Laios was his name, yes.

267
00:12:41,030 --> 00:12:43,170
He was quite the skilled adventurer.

268
00:12:43,530 --> 00:12:46,190
But I wonder just how far he will go.

269
00:12:52,530 --> 00:12:53,930
Good morning, Namaari.

270
00:12:54,950 --> 00:12:56,230
How are you feeling?

271
00:12:57,230 --> 00:12:57,590
Wait!

272
00:12:57,590 --> 00:12:59,070
Where's my ex?

273
00:12:59,870 --> 00:13:01,050
Your stuff is there.

274
00:13:01,970 --> 00:13:04,630
Also, this is from Grandpa Tonsu.

275
00:13:07,510 --> 00:13:08,830
Isn't this too much?

276
00:13:09,070 --> 00:13:10,750
You can think of it as a retainer.

277
00:13:11,030 --> 00:13:12,630
For when he needs you in the future.

278
00:13:13,090 --> 00:13:14,370
Oh, thanks a lot.

279
00:13:14,970 --> 00:13:16,230
I appreciate it.

280
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:18,150
Do you need a town guide?

281
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:22,970
So, where are you staying?

282
00:13:23,330 --> 00:13:24,830
You must be going to rest up.

283
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:25,850
Not yet.

284
00:13:26,070 --> 00:13:27,470
I'm going back to the dungeon.

285
00:13:28,530 --> 00:13:29,370
Oh, my.

286
00:13:29,770 --> 00:13:30,850
You're returning already?

287
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:31,790
No, no.

288
00:13:31,930 --> 00:13:34,010
I just have some business at the temple nearby.

289
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:36,010
Business?

290
00:13:36,530 --> 00:13:37,010
Business.

291
00:13:37,010 --> 00:13:38,010
Revivals.

292
00:13:47,190 --> 00:13:47,670
Revivals.

293
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:48,930
Huh?

294
00:13:48,930 --> 00:13:50,310
Oh, Namaari.

295
00:13:50,970 --> 00:13:53,590
Those are the eyes of someone looking for something.

296
00:13:53,590 --> 00:13:57,790
So, is it a thing or a person?

297
00:13:58,210 --> 00:13:58,690
Person.

298
00:13:59,130 --> 00:14:00,430
A female tall man.

299
00:14:00,630 --> 00:14:01,510
Hair light brown.

300
00:14:01,950 --> 00:14:03,650
Length would be about down to the shoulders.

301
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:05,590
Her age is...

302
00:14:06,190 --> 00:14:08,850
somewhere from teens to forties.

303
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:09,650
Hang on.

304
00:14:09,870 --> 00:14:11,230
Is this Laios' sister?

305
00:14:11,690 --> 00:14:14,190
There's no question that girl is in her twenties.

306
00:14:14,530 --> 00:14:16,050
Go get your eyes checked out.

307
00:14:16,570 --> 00:14:17,490
Give me a break.

308
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:19,050
How should I know, huh?

309
00:14:19,830 --> 00:14:20,310
Hmm.

310
00:14:21,010 --> 00:14:23,710
Nothing by that description has been brought here yet.

311
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:25,190
I see.

312
00:14:27,330 --> 00:14:28,910
The fifth floor.

313
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:33,110
Exiting the Golden Castle leads to the castle town.

314
00:14:33,890 --> 00:14:37,430
The area has expanded and distorted due to magic.

315
00:14:37,430 --> 00:14:40,930
But you can still sense phantoms of its former glory.

316
00:14:41,850 --> 00:14:44,830
A person passing by, just out of sight.

317
00:14:45,710 --> 00:14:47,390
The sound of someone whispering.

318
00:14:48,370 --> 00:14:51,150
These strange feelings linger like a dream.

319
00:14:53,770 --> 00:14:56,350
So this is where the orcs set up their post.

320
00:14:56,990 --> 00:14:59,070
Looks like they left here in a hurry, too.

321
00:14:59,390 --> 00:15:01,350
Their food storage is a complete mess.

322
00:15:01,870 --> 00:15:03,330
What a horrible smell.

323
00:15:03,710 --> 00:15:05,870
Must have been ransacked by nearby monsters.

324
00:15:05,870 --> 00:15:08,750
Looks like the flour and alcohol are okay.

325
00:15:09,370 --> 00:15:09,810
Oh.

326
00:15:10,470 --> 00:15:11,650
Let's bake some bread.

327
00:15:12,130 --> 00:15:14,130
If the orcs come back, they'll be mad.

328
00:15:14,450 --> 00:15:17,510
Ah, we gave them vegetables, so we should be squared away.

329
00:15:17,510 --> 00:15:17,790
Okay.

330
00:15:30,730 --> 00:15:31,210
Wargs.

331
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:34,370
Was this the red dragon?

332
00:15:34,930 --> 00:15:35,690
Seems so.

333
00:15:36,090 --> 00:15:38,350
Looks like they all got hit by its fire-breath attack.

334
00:15:39,890 --> 00:15:41,190
Going by the smoke.

335
00:15:41,570 --> 00:15:43,230
It must have just been here.

336
00:15:43,230 --> 00:15:45,250
Hey, Laios.

337
00:15:45,850 --> 00:15:50,350
I remember you saying that dragons aren't really active, that they mostly sleep a lot.

338
00:15:50,910 --> 00:15:58,930
But going off what the orcs said and seeing all this, it's been moving around ever since, and might even be wandering around nearby.

339
00:15:59,730 --> 00:16:05,410
I think we could have won against a sleeping dragon, but can we really defeat it now?

340
00:16:05,410 --> 00:16:10,410
What if we lose, or what if she's already been digested?

341
00:16:10,410 --> 00:16:14,670
Hey, it's all right. Take a deep breath. Let's just think it all through.

342
00:16:15,190 --> 00:16:19,470
Well, whatever you decide, don't forget you'll have to fight it with just three people.

343
00:16:20,390 --> 00:16:21,010
Just three?

344
00:16:23,550 --> 00:16:27,210
Don't look at me like that! I told you that I'm not built for fighting!

345
00:16:27,630 --> 00:16:30,510
My job was to help get all of you here, and that's all!

346
00:16:30,690 --> 00:16:31,530
We know that.

347
00:16:31,830 --> 00:16:33,150
We weren't blaming you.

348
00:16:33,750 --> 00:16:35,650
I may have overreacted.

349
00:16:35,650 --> 00:16:38,810
So how are you defeating dragons before now?

350
00:16:39,470 --> 00:16:42,830
Well, it depended on a bunch of different factors, but...

351
00:16:42,830 --> 00:16:45,070
Fallon would cast protection spells against fire.

352
00:16:46,010 --> 00:16:48,130
Namari, Shuro, and I would slow its movement.

353
00:16:48,970 --> 00:16:50,950
Marcil would weaken it with explosion magic.

354
00:16:51,450 --> 00:16:53,530
And Shuro would deliver the final blow.

355
00:16:54,570 --> 00:16:56,670
I think that's how it would go, at least.

356
00:16:56,670 --> 00:17:00,550
But that's not gonna work with the party we have now, though.

357
00:17:01,170 --> 00:17:03,950
We have to think of a plan that'll work for the three of us.

358
00:17:04,970 --> 00:17:10,170
Dragons are covered in super-tough scales, making them resistant to magic and weapons.

359
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:15,410
But under its neck, there's an inverse scale that serves as its weak spot.

360
00:17:15,950 --> 00:17:17,630
If we strike there, we can win.

361
00:17:18,110 --> 00:17:19,150
Under the neck?

362
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:22,790
And about how big would you say this red dragon is, exactly?

363
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:24,790
How to explain...

364
00:17:24,790 --> 00:17:26,270
Oh! See that there?

365
00:17:27,090 --> 00:17:29,470
It's about as tall as that crumbled passageway.

366
00:17:30,230 --> 00:17:34,190
I mean, that literally looks like the dragon bonked its head there.

367
00:17:34,550 --> 00:17:35,950
Oh, that makes sense.

368
00:17:36,750 --> 00:17:37,850
It's quite huge.

369
00:17:38,270 --> 00:17:41,150
It'll be no easy task, striking the scale from that height.

370
00:17:41,390 --> 00:17:42,790
Yeah, you are not kidding.

371
00:17:43,810 --> 00:17:44,370
Hmm.

372
00:17:45,090 --> 00:17:46,630
Let's try getting up there.

373
00:17:49,290 --> 00:17:50,770
It's pretty high up.

374
00:17:50,770 --> 00:17:53,450
What if we jumped on the dragon's neck from here?

375
00:17:53,630 --> 00:17:54,510
You can't do that!

376
00:17:54,550 --> 00:17:55,330
What she said.

377
00:17:55,850 --> 00:17:59,770
I can cast Abjuration Spells, but they won't be as good as Falon's.

378
00:18:00,090 --> 00:18:04,290
If you fall from this height, you'll definitely hurt yourself, and it'll all be over.

379
00:18:04,710 --> 00:18:05,730
And that's not all.

380
00:18:05,970 --> 00:18:07,150
What about its fire breath?

381
00:18:07,510 --> 00:18:08,950
None of us can outrun that.

382
00:18:09,370 --> 00:18:09,870
Oh, yeah.

383
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:13,850
Namaari also said that Senshi's axe won't stand a chance against it.

384
00:18:14,230 --> 00:18:15,830
What about your weapon, Laios?

385
00:18:16,770 --> 00:18:20,430
You'd have to keep it occupied while I'm charging up a strong explosion spell.

386
00:18:20,810 --> 00:18:22,170
One that will knock it unconscious.

387
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:25,750
And after that, someone will have to fatally wound it.

388
00:18:26,110 --> 00:18:28,730
Do you think you and Senshi can pull all of that off?

389
00:18:29,190 --> 00:18:29,830
Of course.

390
00:18:30,190 --> 00:18:31,270
I'm sure we can.

391
00:18:31,450 --> 00:18:32,330
Okay, how?

392
00:18:33,670 --> 00:18:34,130
Oh.

393
00:18:34,130 --> 00:18:39,830
Instead of hitting the dragon, what if we were to blow up a structure instead?

394
00:18:40,830 --> 00:18:44,050
There are lots of houses and bridges that extend between buildings.

395
00:18:45,190 --> 00:18:50,190
We blow one up when the dragon goes and walks under it, and the rubble should slow down its movement.

396
00:18:50,690 --> 00:18:55,290
With all that rubble weighing it down, the inverse scale will be within striking distance.

397
00:18:55,290 --> 00:18:59,730
We won't be able to buy much time when we're actually fighting it.

398
00:19:00,470 --> 00:19:03,810
But we can lure it somewhere we want while we're running away from it.

399
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:06,270
These paths are narrow for a red dragon.

400
00:19:07,230 --> 00:19:09,610
It should also be tired from being so active.

401
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:13,350
With the proper route, we can tire it out even more.

402
00:19:13,350 --> 00:19:14,610
I see.

403
00:19:14,930 --> 00:19:16,730
Well, I can probably help with that, then.

404
00:19:17,090 --> 00:19:17,390
Really?

405
00:19:17,770 --> 00:19:19,130
Thank you, too, Doug.

406
00:19:19,190 --> 00:19:20,050
I'm so happy!

407
00:19:20,470 --> 00:19:22,970
I wonder why the dragon's not sleeping, though.

408
00:19:23,290 --> 00:19:25,390
And why'd it show up on Floor 5?

409
00:19:25,670 --> 00:19:28,870
It seems to be wandering around narrow areas that it doesn't like.

410
00:19:29,310 --> 00:19:30,650
Maybe it's mating time?

411
00:19:31,030 --> 00:19:31,810
Probably not.

412
00:19:32,030 --> 00:19:33,230
Oh, hang on a sec.

413
00:19:33,430 --> 00:19:36,810
Didn't Amari say Senshi's pen is made out of a really cool metal?

414
00:19:37,170 --> 00:19:37,790
What was it?

415
00:19:37,850 --> 00:19:41,610
Something about blocking the dragon's fangs and smashing through its bones, I think?

416
00:19:41,730 --> 00:19:42,130
Oh!

417
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:43,370
That's right!

418
00:19:43,450 --> 00:19:45,650
She said that blacksmiths dream about this stuff!

419
00:19:45,890 --> 00:19:48,790
If that's true, it must be able to block its fire breath.

420
00:19:48,850 --> 00:19:49,530
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

421
00:19:49,830 --> 00:19:52,250
Well, that's one of our problems taken care of.

422
00:19:52,530 --> 00:19:55,110
Sure, that knife isn't also made from something special.

423
00:19:55,770 --> 00:19:57,910
We should have had Amari look at it, huh?

424
00:19:58,370 --> 00:20:00,570
I'm starting to feel like we can do this.

425
00:20:00,910 --> 00:20:03,210
Like they say, if there's a will, there's a way.

426
00:20:03,530 --> 00:20:03,890
Right.

427
00:20:04,330 --> 00:20:06,170
Let's finish planning out our attack.

428
00:20:06,810 --> 00:20:26,710
Oh, you're back.

429
00:20:27,250 --> 00:20:28,890
Senshi, why did you wander off?

430
00:20:28,970 --> 00:20:30,190
We were wondering where you went.

431
00:20:30,510 --> 00:20:31,590
I was making bread.

432
00:20:32,010 --> 00:20:34,470
You know we're about to fight a dragon, don't you?

433
00:20:34,910 --> 00:20:35,590
Of course.

434
00:20:35,590 --> 00:20:38,030
This will be quite the task, don't you think?

435
00:20:38,490 --> 00:20:40,430
A good meal is most important.

436
00:20:42,150 --> 00:20:45,350
We've already lost once to this dragon because of an empty stomach.

437
00:20:45,950 --> 00:20:47,430
This time will be different.

438
00:20:47,850 --> 00:20:48,190
Right?

439
00:20:49,130 --> 00:20:50,070
There's wine!

440
00:20:50,810 --> 00:20:53,110
I went and borrowed a few things from the pantry.

441
00:20:54,810 --> 00:20:56,670
Not until we beat the dragon.

442
00:20:56,670 --> 00:21:00,770
We don't have any eggs, but we should still be able to make that.

443
00:21:03,250 --> 00:21:05,130
Shave down some bread with a grater.

444
00:21:06,090 --> 00:21:08,730
Season the giant frog meat with salt and pepper.

445
00:21:09,430 --> 00:21:11,990
Dip the meat in a water and flour mixture.

446
00:21:12,670 --> 00:21:13,810
Work in the breadcrumbs.

447
00:21:14,370 --> 00:21:16,590
Then heat some olive oil and fry.

448
00:21:16,590 --> 00:21:23,050
Boil down some bread, wine, and seasonings to make a sauce.

449
00:21:26,650 --> 00:21:27,710
It's ready.

450
00:21:30,430 --> 00:21:31,570
Looks delicious.

451
00:21:31,570 --> 00:21:34,670
Once I started smelling it, I got really hungry.

452
00:21:35,130 --> 00:21:36,270
Let's do it again, everyone!

453
00:21:38,350 --> 00:21:39,670
It's so crispy.

454
00:21:43,590 --> 00:21:44,650
What's wrong, Marcel?

455
00:21:45,350 --> 00:21:49,470
Knowing these monster meals will come to an end soon just got me a little emotional.

456
00:21:49,470 --> 00:21:51,750
Well, let's not get ahead of ourselves.

457
00:21:57,550 --> 00:21:59,650
Everyone, I want to say something.

458
00:22:00,690 --> 00:22:03,870
I don't think I would have been able to make it this far on my own.

459
00:22:04,670 --> 00:22:06,330
Senshi, thank you.

460
00:22:07,150 --> 00:22:09,770
We were strangers, but you were still kind to us.

461
00:22:10,290 --> 00:22:13,850
Your food not only filled our stomachs, but my heart as well.

462
00:22:13,850 --> 00:22:19,630
Chilchuk, if you weren't with us, we would have lost days taking the long way down.

463
00:22:20,030 --> 00:22:21,370
That helped us so much.

464
00:22:22,330 --> 00:22:26,250
And Marcel, I'm sorry for putting you through everything.

465
00:22:26,750 --> 00:22:29,730
When you said you'd come with us, I was really happy.

466
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:33,610
Everyone, thank you so much.

467
00:22:37,390 --> 00:22:38,630
Of course!

468
00:22:39,070 --> 00:22:40,070
You're so cringe!

469
00:22:40,350 --> 00:22:40,870
Sorry.

470
00:22:43,850 --> 00:23:05,930
It's even bigger than I remembered it being.

471
00:23:06,330 --> 00:23:07,130
No kidding.

472
00:23:07,510 --> 00:23:08,970
Can we really defeat that?

473
00:23:09,970 --> 00:23:10,190
What?

474
00:23:10,890 --> 00:23:11,710
We'll be fine.

475
00:23:11,710 --> 00:23:13,710
We all got this far, didn't we?

476
00:23:14,470 --> 00:23:15,810
Let's review the plan.

477
00:23:16,430 --> 00:23:19,610
Marcel has her spot, which we'll lure the dragon to.

478
00:23:20,590 --> 00:23:21,450
Is everyone ready?

479
00:23:22,350 --> 00:23:24,090
Seems our health is in good shape.

480
00:23:25,290 --> 00:23:25,890
All right.

481
00:23:27,110 --> 00:23:27,970
Let's go!

